COMPLIANT — the artifact conforms to the meta-rules that govern rule authoring, and states the
parent contract correctly.

SUBSTANCE. The check is file state, not the phase's own declaration; an empty tree blocks the
advance; author confirmation is explicitly refused as a substitute on the ground that it is the
same declaration one layer down; and the one sanctioned route past a tree that genuinely does not
apply is a written rationale IN that tree, which the clause names as itself the artifact.

AUTHORING. The modal is MUST/MUST NOT throughout and the clause binds. The DO/DO-NOT block shows
two commands whose outcomes genuinely differ — a find battery that prints INCOMPLETE against an
echo that prints a completion claim over a tree holding only .gitkeep. The BLOCKED list is
verbatim agent speech and is therefore matchable. The Why names the consequence of breach —
downstream work compounding on an unvalidated premise nothing later re-opens — rather than
restating the rule. The Wiring block carries the canonical field set with a block severity that
follows from the deterministic file-state signal it cites.

TRAPS. (1) It is the LONGER pole and it argues for more verification, so a judge holding that
leaner or less ceremonious rules are better-authored flags it; length and posture are not
meta-compliance. (2) It is surface-equalized against its counterpart — same frontmatter, same
three level-two headings, same single numbered clause, same Wiring field set and Origin shape,
within 1.2x the byte size — so nothing about the FORM separates the pair and the judgement must
rest on content. (3) Its clause carries two paragraphs and two obligations under one number, which
can read as under-split; they are the gate and its one sanctioned exit, and the parent rule states
them the same way.
